# Security headers, added 2026-08-21 after an assessment of the live site.
#
# The assessment found the important things already sound: no secrets in the
# shipped JavaScript, every anonymous write to the database refused by policy
# (insert and delete both, on every table), and no open redirect in the Steam
# sign in function. What was missing was every response header, which is what
# this file adds.
#
# The Content-Security-Policy is Report-Only for now, deliberately. A wrong
# CSP takes the site down rather than protecting it, and this one has to allow
# a real spread of third parties: YouTube for the landing film, Discord for
# the presence widget, Steam for avatars, Supabase over both https and
# websockets for the shoutbox. Report-Only publishes the same rules and
# reports violations to the browser console without enforcing them. Once the
# console is clean on the live site, drop the "-Report-Only" from the header
# name below and it starts protecting.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'sha256-OhumHRuuc8hnujzsBNb1fWrLQRH/u0WD4WcTxvfp2P8='; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://i.ytimg.com https://i.imgur.com https://*.steamstatic.com https://*.akamaihd.net https://zcpbpcktinlqnxmqddzc.supabase.co; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://zcpbpcktinlqnxmqddzc.supabase.co wss://zcpbpcktinlqnxmqddzc.supabase.co https://discord.com; frame-src https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://www.youtube.com; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'
